<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>This tab is for Admins and people with the CanManageFiles role.</FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Deleted files and folders">
        <FluentText>
            Deleting a file or folder puts it in the <strong>Recycle bin</strong> (in Quick access). A folder goes with
            everything in it. Each item shows where it came from, who deleted it and when it will be deleted for good.
            While it's in the bin, nobody can open or download it, even from a link they saved, unless something in
            Lanyard still uses it.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Restore</strong> puts it back where it was. If that folder has been deleted too, it goes to the top
            level instead, and if the name has been used since, it's restored with a number added. Lanyard tells you
            when either happens.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Deleting for good">
        <FluentText>
            Items are deleted for good 30 days after they went in the bin. To do it sooner, use the bin icon beside an
            item, or <strong>Empty bin</strong> for everything. This can't be undone.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
            A file that's still in use, such as the company logo, an onboarding email attachment or a projection
            program's video, is never deleted for good while something uses it. It stays in the bin and keeps
            working until you change what uses it.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
